A diagnostic run executes the code as written:
const arr = [500, 2, 3];
console.log(arr.includes(500));
In this run, what does the log show?

The console output of this snippet is in question:
const arr = [501, 2, 1];
arr.push(56);
console.log(arr.length);
In this run, what number is printed by the final log?

A test harness runs these statements in order:
const arr = [502, 26, 59, 15];
const part = arr.slice(1, 3);
console.log(part.length);
What is the length of part after the slice call?

A student submits the snippet below for review:
const arr = [503, 14, 41, 53, 92];
const removed = arr.splice(1, 2);
console.log(arr.length);
