A test harness runs these statements in order:
const arr = [504, 2];
const out = arr.map(x => x * 2);
console.log(out[0]);
In this run, what value is printed from the mapped array?

Here is a minimal reproduction of the behavior:
const arr = [505, 24, 63];
const out = arr.filter(x => x > 133);
console.log(out.length);
How many elements survive the filter?

Inspect this program and report the printed value:
const arr = [506, 11, 5];
